#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working with Frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: frames.docbook:12 frames.docbook:73 frames.docbook:86 frames.docbook:189
#: frames.docbook:227 frames.docbook:253 frames.docbook:297 frames.docbook:327
#: frames.docbook:328 frames.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "frames"
msgstr "imatges"

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:12 frames.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "introduction"
msgstr "introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since &kword; is a frames based word processor, an understanding of frames "
"and framesets is necessary for all but the most simple of documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section is designed to give you a firm understanding of how to create, "
"destroy and manipulate frames so &kword; can provide you with the exact "
"document you want."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "Framesets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: frames.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "framesets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before we continue our discussion of Frames, its important that we define a "
"couple terms now:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: frames.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frame"
msgstr "Encastre"

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A frame is a rectangular space on the page. This space defines an area where "
"text (or other data), can be placed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: frames.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frameset"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A frameset is a group of frames. Each frame in the frameset has a position "
"within the frameset"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The position is determined by their placement on the page. If frames extend "
"across the entire width of the page, the frame which begins closest to the "
"top of the page is Frame #1. The next frame that is closest to the top of "
"the page is Frame #2, etc. If the frames do not extend across the width of "
"the page, the frame whose left edge is closest to the left margin will be "
"frame #1. In this case, the vertical position of the frame is ignored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All text flows from one frame to another <emphasis>within a frameset, and "
"only within a frameset.</emphasis> Text flows from frame to frame within the "
"frameset <emphasis>according to the position of each frame</emphasis> on the "
"page (and therefore the order of the frames within the frameset)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As an example: If we have a frameset that consists of three frames (#1, #2, "
"and #3)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As we type text into Frame #1, the text is shaped to the outline of Frame #1."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the text will no longer fit within Frame #1, it is automatically "
"continued into Frame #2."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Text moves freely between frames within a frameset. If you insert text in "
"the middle of a frame, all text after the inserted text is rearranged as you "
"type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting a frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "selecting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can select a frame within a frameset two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "By clicking on the text frame border of the frame you want to select."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "By holding down the &Ctrl; key and clicking anywhere within the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "There should now be 8 squares around the edges of the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding a Text Frame to a Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "adding a text frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding a text frame can be done one of three ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Text Frame</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo><keycap>F10</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or by clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref="
"\"tfcreatebut.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on "
"the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whatever method you choose, &kword; responds by changing the cursor to a set "
"of cross hairs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the mouse, place the crosshairs at the desired position of the upper "
"left corner of the new text frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click once with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alternative, first position the text caret at the place where you want to "
"insert the frame. When the mouse cursor changes to crosshairs, press &Enter;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "A dialog box appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog box is used to determine which frameset this new frame will "
"belong to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the screenshot as an example, a new text frame has been created in a "
"document which currently has two framesets (called <guilabel>Text Frameset "
"1</guilabel>, and <guilabel>Text Frameset 2</guilabel>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "You now have the option of either:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: frames.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add the new frame to one of the previously created framesets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To do this, simply select the frameset you want the new frame to belong to. "
"(Either <guilabel>Text Frameset 1</guilabel>, or <guilabel>Text Frameset 2</"
"guilabel> in the example.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this text frame is created, the new text frame will become a member of "
"the selected frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: frames.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a new frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want this to be a new frameset, you should enter a descriptive name "
"for your new frameset. (A name which will tell you what you might find in "
"that frameset). This name should be entered in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Name of frameset:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "This newly added frame will be the only frame in the frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The other tabs in this dialog box, can be used to set some options for this "
"frame. For more information on these options, see the section entitled <link "
"linkend=\"format-frame\">Setting the properties for a frame</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>, the new frame will be created."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton>, the new frame will not be "
"created, and you will be returned to editing your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, &kword; creates a small frame with the upper left corner of the "
"frame located on the page where you clicked with the mouse cursor. After the "
"frame is created, you are expected to reshape the frame to fit your needs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you would prefer to establish the shape of your frame <emphasis>while you "
"are creating</emphasis> the frame, simply click the &LMB; where you want the "
"upper left corner to be placed and hold the button down. Drag the mouse "
"towards the opposite corner of the frame to establish the boundaries of the "
"new frame. As you drag the mouse, you will see a box drawn. This box "
"represents the boundaries of your new text frame. When you are satisfied "
"with the size and shape of the new text frame, release the mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a Frame From a Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "deleting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may decide you no longer need a frame in your document. You could leave "
"it blank (so it would not be visible in the final output), but you should "
"delete it to keep your document as simple as possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Begin by clicking on the text frame border of the frame you want to delete. "
"(Or holding down the &Ctrl; key and clicking inside the frame with the "
"&LMB;.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:200 frames.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are now 8 squares on the edges of the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "If this is the frame you want to delete, you can do so by:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "Press the <keycap>Delete</keycap> key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Delete Frame</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While the cursor is on the border of the frame you want to delete, click "
"once with the &RMB;. A small menu will appear. Select <guimenuitem>Delete "
"Frame</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving a Frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "moving"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving a frame around on the page is easy."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Begin by clicking on the text frame border of the frame you want to move. "
"(Or holding down the &Ctrl; key and clicking inside the frame with the "
"&LMB;.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click and hold the &LMB; on the border again and drag the cursor in the "
"direction you want to move the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will see an outline of the frame as you move it. When the outline is "
"where you want it, release the mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A faster way to move the frame, can be done by holding down the &Ctrl; and "
"&Shift; keys on the keyboard and click and hold with the &LMB;. Drag the "
"mouse cursor on the page and when the frame is in the correct location, "
"release the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "Resizing a Frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "resizing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid "It is also easy to change the size or shape of a frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Begin by clicking on the text frame border of the frame you want to change. "
"(Or holding down the &Ctrl; key and clicking inside the frame with the "
"&LMB;.) This selects this frame as the current frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are now 8 squares on the edges of the frame. By moving these squares, "
"you will be able to drag the frame border(s) to a new location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each square will move a different combination of borders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As an example: To move the bottom border of a frame, place the mouse over "
"the box at the six o'clock position in the frame. When the mouse is over the "
"box, it will change to a double headed arrow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now click with the &LMB; and hold the button down. As you move the mouse up "
"and down on the page, you will see that the frame changes shape to match the "
"movements of the mouse. When the bottom edge of the frame is at the new "
"location, simply release the mouse button, and the changes will become "
"permanent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are using a Text Oriented Template, you cannot change the size of the "
"primary frame by dragging the edges of the frame. If you want to resize this "
"frame, you must do so by <link linkend=\"page-format\">Changing the margins</"
"link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reconnecting Frames in a Frameset/Changing text flow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "create/edit framesets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Normally, each new text frame is created with a specific purpose. Sometimes, "
"however, as the document is changed, changes to the text flow will need to "
"be made. To accomplish this, you will need to know how to move a frame from "
"one frameset to another."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First click on the frame border of the frame you want to move to another "
"frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the frameset of the currently selected frame by selecting "
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame/Frameset "
"Properties</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also accomplish this by clicking on the frame border once with the "
"&RMB;, and selecting <guilabel>Frame/Frameset Properties...</guilabel> from "
"the popup menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will bring up a dialog box with five tabs. Select the tab labeled "
"<guilabel>Connect Text Frames</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will be presented with a list of framesets. Simply select the new "
"frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>, the currently selected frame will "
"be added to that frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "Raise and Lower Frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "raise"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "lower"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When two frames occupy the same place on a page, they must overlap. When "
"they overlap, one frame sits <emphasis>above</emphasis> the other frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can raise and lower the frames to change which frame sits above the "
"other frames by using four commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: frames.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bring to Front"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:337 frames.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To raise a frame, select the frame by clicking once on the frame border with "
"the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Bring to Front</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will place the frame on top of <emphasis>all other frames</emphasis> "
"that it overlaps."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: frames.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "Raise Frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Raise Frame</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will move the frame up <emphasis>one level</emphasis> of any frame that "
"it overlaps."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>R</keycap></"
"keycombo> is the same as selecting <guilabel>Raise Frame</guilabel> from the "
"menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: frames.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Send to Back"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:359 frames.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To lower a frame, select the frame by clicking once on the frame border with "
"the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Send to Back</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will place the frame below <emphasis>all other frames</emphasis> that "
"it overlaps."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: frames.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lower Frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Lower Frame</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will move the frame down <emphasis>one level</emphasis> of any frame "
"that it overlaps."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>L</keycap></"
"keycombo> is the same as selecting <guilabel>Lower Frame</guilabel> from the "
"menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: frames.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hard Frame Breaks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: frames.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "frame breaks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: frames.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "page breaks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A hard frame break is a special formatting character. It is invisible on the "
"final printed output."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The purpose of a hard frame break, is to force all the text that follows it "
"into the next frame in the frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If we have the following sentence: <quote>We have nothing to fear but fear "
"itself</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"and we insert a Hard Frame Break, just before the word <quote>but</quote>, "
"we will end up with one frame containing <quote>We have nothing to fear</"
"quote>, and the next frame in the frameset beginning with <quote>but fear "
"itself</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a Hard Frame Break, you should first place the keyboard cursor where "
"you want the break to be located in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Hard Frame Break can be inserted one of two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Page Break</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo><keycap>Ctrl</"
"keycap><keycap>Return</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to remove a Hard Frame Break, you simply delete it like you "
"would any other character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since this is not a character that you can normally see in &kword;, it will "
"be easier to delete a Hard Frame Break with the following procedure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Formatting "
"Characters</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. This will make the "
"breaks visible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Find the newly revealed Page Break, labeled <guilabel>--- Frame Break ---</"
"guilabel>. Place the mouse pointer in front of this and click once with the "
"&LMB;. This will place the cursor directly in front of the page break."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: frames.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now press the <keycap>Delete</keycap> key."
msgstr ""
